= Hu Hanmin

Though one of the "elder" statesmen of the KMT, Hu Hanmin was sidelined and sent into effective exile (as a "representative" of the KMT to the Comintern) after being implicated in the assassination of Liao Zhongkai. His time in the Soviet Union, however, has hardened his previously ambivalent attitude towards the Communists, and enforced his self-declared role as the chief theorist of Orthodox Tridemism.

